<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Assignment 6.1 — Box Model Inspection</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

    <header class="header">
        <h1>Box Model Inspection Lab</h1>
        <p>Analyze how padding, borders, margins, and the <code>box-sizing</code> property control element dimensions.</p>
    </header>

    <main class="container">
        
        <!-- Box 1: Content-Box Demonstration -->
        <div class="box box-content">
            <h2>Box 1: Content Box</h2>
            <p><strong>Behavior:</strong> Uses <code>box-sizing: content-box</code> (the browser default). Padding and borders are added <em>on top</em> of the 250px width. Total width = 250px + 40px padding + 10px border = 300px.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Box 2: Border-Box Demonstration -->
        <div class="box box-border">
            <h2>Box 2: Border Box</h2>
            <p><strong>Behavior:</strong> Uses <code>box-sizing: border-box</code>. Padding and borders are absorbed <em>inside</em> the 250px width. Total width remains exactly 250px. The space for content shrinks to accommodate them.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Box 3: Spacing & Margin Shift -->
        <div class="box box-margin">
            <h2>Box 3: Extreme Spacing</h2>
            <p><strong>Behavior:</strong> Implements aggressive margin tracking to push neighboring layouts away. Open your DevTools inspector to view how the orange outer layer generates physical space.</p>
        </div>

    </main>

    <div class="guide-panel">
        <h3>DevTools Homework Guide</h3>
        <p>Right-click any box, choose <strong>Inspect</strong>, and scroll to the bottom of the <strong>Computed</strong> styles panel to view your active box model diagram. Take your screenshot there!</p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>







/* ==========================================
   BASE LAYOUT CONFIGURATION
   ========================================== */
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

body {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    background-color: #f1f5f9;
    color: #1e293b;
    padding: 40px 20px;
    line-height: 1.5;
}

.header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
}

.header h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
}

.container {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 20px;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
}

/* ==========================================
   BOX STRUCTURAL EXPERIMENTS
   ========================================== */
.box {
    width: 250px; /* Base static width applied to all blocks */
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: 4px;
}

.box h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: #0f172a;
}

.box p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #475569;
}

/* --- Box 1: Content Box Rules --- */
.box-content {
    box-sizing: content-box; /* Browser default structural setting */
    padding: 20px;
    border: 5px solid #3b82f6; /* Blue border */
    margin: 15px;
}

/* --- Box 2: Border Box Rules --- */
.box-border {
    box-sizing: border-box; /* Forces layout to absorb inside dimensions */
    padding: 20px;
    border: 5px solid #10b981; /* Green border */
    margin: 15px;
}

/* --- Box 3: Spacing & Margin Shift Rules --- */
.box-margin {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 35px;             /* Massive interior padding expansion */
    border: 10px solid #f59e0b; /* Amber thick border */
    margin: 45px;              /* Massive exterior push back footprint */
}

/* ==========================================
   INSTRUCTIONAL ASSISTANCE PANEL
   ========================================== */
.guide-panel {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 40px auto 0 auto;
    background-color: #e0f2fe;
    border-left: 4px solid #0284c7;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 4px;
}

.guide-panel h3 {
    color: #0369a1;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
}






